# Godot Executable Path

When running Godot commands from the agent, do not call bare `godot` unless no configured editor path can be found.

Before invoking Godot, resolve the executable from Cursor user settings:

- Read `%APPDATA%\Cursor\User\settings.json`.
- Use `godotTools.editorPath.godot4` as the Godot executable path.
- Invoke it explicitly, quoted, for all Godot CLI/headless checks.

Example PowerShell shape:

```powershell
$settings = Get-Content "$env:APPDATA\Cursor\User\settings.json" | ConvertFrom-Json
$godot = $settings.'godotTools.editorPath.godot4'
& $godot --headless --path "<project-path>" --script "res://some_check.gd"
```

If the setting is missing or the executable path does not exist, tell the user before falling back to `godot` on `PATH`.
